{#- Today's special sides, for the counter (client 2026-10-29: two sides
    added last minute, the plate comes with one of them or any regular
    side). The day is `sidesDate` above, read from specials.json, so the
    plate and the sides are the ones Square has: its `sides` is one entry
    with "or" between ("Oven Browned Potatoes or Twice Baked Potato
    Casserole"), which is one side the customer picks. Two entries are two
    sides the plate comes with (client 2026-10-30: Mac & Cheese and Baked
    Beans), and the sign says "both", that a customer can double up on one
    and that each is sold separately; the day needs the same two in
    `extraSides`, which is what puts each on the other's list in Square.
    For another day, change the date, check the day's sides read one of
    those ways, build, print.
    The regular sides box is the Deli Salads (menu.json) and the soup, the
    same swap list as Lunch Special's Side 1 in Square. No logo (client
    2026-10-29: it stands on the counter, so the name is redundant there);
    the room it took goes to bigger type. -#}
{%- set d = (specials.days | where("date", sidesDate))[0] %}
{%- set sidesCat = (menu.categories | where("id", "sides"))[0] %}
{%- set deli = (sidesCat.items | selectattr("choices") | first) if sidesCat else null %}
{%- set both = d and d.sides.length > 1 %}
<div class="canvas sign sign--bw ts{% if both %} ts--both{% endif %}">
    <div class="sign-heading">
        <h2 class="p-display sign-heading-title">Today&rsquo;s Special Sides</h2>
    </div>

    {%- if d %}
    <p class="p-display ts-plate">{{ d.special }}</p>
    {%- if both %}
    <p class="ts-one">comes with <strong>both</strong> sides:</p>
    {%- else %}
    <p class="ts-one">comes with <strong>one</strong> side. Pick from:</p>
    {%- endif %}

    <div class="ts-picks">
        {%- for s in (d.sides if both else (d.sides[0] or "").split(" or ")) %}
        {%- if not loop.first %}
        <p class="ts-or">{{ "and" if both else "or" }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
        <p class="p-display ts-pick">{{ s }}</p>
        {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    {%- if both %}
    <p class="ts-more">Like one better? Double up on it.</p>
    <p class="ts-more">Each side is also sold separately.</p>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endif %}

    <div class="sign-spacer"></div>
    {%- if deli %}
    <section class="sw-choice ts-regular">
        <p class="p-display sw-choice-title">{% if both %}Or swap a side for any of these{% else %}Or any of our regular sides{% endif %}</p>
        <ul class="sw-choices">
            {%- for c in deli.choices %}
            <li>{{ c }}</li>
            {%- endfor %}
            {%- if specials.soupSide %}
            <li>Cup of the day&rsquo;s soup</li>
            {%- endif %}
        </ul>
    </section>
    {%- endif %}
</div>
